wifi-nightmare (3.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * PMKID Attack: clientless WPA2 hash harvesting for Hashcat mode 22000.
  * Karma Attack: auto-respond to 802.11 Probe Requests to attract clients.
  * Beacon Flooding: high-frequency 802.11 Beacon storm with custom SSIDs.
  * WPA-Enterprise Fake RADIUS: rogue 802.1X AP harvesting PEAP/TTLS credentials.
  * Smart Wordlists & Auto-Rockyou: SSID-aware candidate generation + ISP defaults.
  * Session Export: JSON, CSV, and human-readable report export.
  * Rich TUI Live Dashboard: real-time scanner with RSSI bars and security badges.
  * Geo-Location BSSID Lookup: resolve AP location via Wigle.net and OpenWifi APIs.
  * Multi-Card Aggregation Engine: dedicated Sniffer + Injector role assignment.
  * Dual-Band Scanning: 2.4 GHz + 5 GHz channel hopping simultaneously.
  * WPA3/SAE Transition Downgrade Attack: force fallback to WPA2-PSK via CSA.
  * Multi-Vector Eviction: bypass 802.11w PMF via CSA and BTM requests.
  * WPS PBC Sniffer: capture WPA-PSK on physical WPS button press.
  * Algorithmic Known-PINs: offline ComputePIN, D-Link, EasyBox generators.
  * WPA3 & PMF Detection in live scanner.
  * Redesigned 2-column horizontal grid UI with per-option descriptions.
  * Monitor mode now uses airmon-ng as primary method (iw as fallback).
  * Automatic monitor interface name detection from airmon-ng output.

 -- Youssef Alkhodary <youssef@alkhodary.com>  Fri, 17 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

wifi-nightmare (2.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Captive portal now triggers on Android 14/15, Samsung One UI 6/7, iOS, ColorOS, Xiaomi MIUI, Vivo Funtouch.
  * Disabled DHCP option 114 when no valid HTTPS tunnel (cloudflared) is active.
  * Port 443 rejected with TCP Reset so HTTPS-first probes fall back to HTTP immediately.
  * All OS probe paths (Android, Apple, Samsung, Oppo, Xiaomi, Vivo) respond with 302 Found + Location header.
  * Fixed captive portal incorrectly rejecting correct passwords: removed -b/-e ESSID filters from aircrack-ng verify.
  * Fixed deauth failing with single-card setup (TL-WN722N v1 / Atheros AR9271): VIF AP + monitor interfaces created simultaneously.
  * Fixed hidden SSID not persisting in menu after reveal.
  * Fixed BSSID fully displayed in Deauth and other outputs.
  * Fixed Evil Twin password capture stripping leading/trailing spaces.
  * Added Option 9 in target menu: crack handshake with aircrack-ng + wordlist (live output, saves to cracked.txt).

 -- Youssef Alkhodary <youssef@alkhodary.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:35:00 +0000

wifi-nightmare (2.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BSSID masking for privacy: all BSSIDs shown as first/last octet only across the TUI and exported files.
  * Export files named by SSID instead of full BSSID (handshakes, pixie dust logs, hc22000).
  * Faster handshake capture: kick-once + long silent window strategy, 1s polling, deauth tool errors surfaced.
  * Pixie Dust: accurate WPS lock-state detection from wash, quote-stripped PIN/PSK parsing, failure diagnosis.
  * VIF support check: PHY-scoped iw list parsing, no more false multi-interface support reports.
  * Removed emoji icons from all menus.

